# Tests before commit

When a change affects behaviour, add or update a test in `game/tests/` that fails on the old behaviour and passes on the new one. A behaviour change without a matching test is unfinished.

Before every commit, run the full suite on the tree being committed and wait for it to finish:

```
~/.local/bin/godot --headless --path game res://tests/run_tests.tscn
```

A new failure blocks the commit. Fix it, or adjust the test when the new behaviour is the one the test should lock in, then re-run the full suite. A known unrelated failure may remain only when it is already recorded (the livery step where Tab lands on the Remove button). Docs-only edits need no new test, and still require the suite before a commit that includes them.
